 "note_en": "Doubling a one-syllable verb with 了 in between, as in 闻了闻 \"took a sniff,\" shows a quick, light action that's already done: 她拿起一瓶，闻了闻 \"she picked up a bottle and gave it a sniff.\" English needs a phrase like \"give it a sniff\" or \"take a quick look\" to say the same thing. Compare 闻起来 in the next line: 这瓶闻起来太甜了 \"this one smells too sweet,\" where 起来 means \"when you smell it.\"",
